  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pdfcpu/pdfcpu/tarball/v0.16.3",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pdfcpu/pdfcpu/zipball/v0.16.3",
  "body": "# pdfcpu v0.16.3\r\n\r\nThis is a security update fixing configured decoded-byte limit bypasses and restricting local image access in create and form input.\r\n\r\n**Applications handling untrusted PDFs or create/form input should upgrade.**\r\n\r\n**Decoded-byte limits — [GHSA-jp42-qm45-2x6g](https://github.com/pdfcpu/pdfcpu/security/advisories/GHSA-jp42-qm45-2x6g):**\r\n\r\nHonor `Limits.MaxDecodeBytes` across stream decoding and combined page content, and stop cross-reference repair after\r\nlimit failures. Strengthen Flate predictor, DCT and cached-content checks, with regression coverage for strict/relaxed\r\nvalidation and eager/deferred decoding.\r\n\r\nThe limit bounds individual decoded streams and combined page content, not total process memory.\r\n\r\n**Additive Go API change:** Add `StreamDict.DecodeWithLimit` and `StreamDict.DecodeLengthWithLimit` to supply the\r\nconfigured decode limit explicitly.\r\n\r\n**Local image access — [GHSA-44h9-p34h-2w4p](https://github.com/pdfcpu/pdfcpu/security/advisories/GHSA-44h9-p34h-2w4p):**\r\n\r\nConfine local images referenced by `create`, `form fill`, and JSON/CSV `form multifill` input to an allowed directory.\r\nReject absolute paths, parent-directory components, symlink escapes and non-regular files, and report access denials\r\nas errors.\r\n\r\n**Compatibility change:** \r\nAPI callers must set `conf.LocalImageRoot` to enable local images; an empty value disables\r\nthem. The CLI defaults to its working directory; set `localImageRoot` in `config.yml` to select another root.\r\nUpdate image paths to be relative to that root. Confined local images are unavailable on `js/wasm`.\r\nSee [local image access](https://pdfcpu.io/create/create/#local-image-access) for migration guidance and limitations.\r\n\r\n**Documentation:** \r\nUpdated [security policy](https://github.com/pdfcpu/pdfcpu/blob/v0.16.3/SECURITY.md) clarifies vulnerability scope, supported releases and guidance for AI-assisted reports and multiple findings. \r\nUpdated [pull request template](https://github.com/pdfcpu/pdfcpu/blob/v0.16.3/.github/pull_request_template.md) clarifies contribution requirements.\r\nAdded local image configuration and migration guidance to README and website.\r\n\r\nRequires Go 1.26 or later, unchanged from v0.16.2.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 35ea259eb27d5a607f797edd41fd8a9e50a1f818 bump version\r\n* 8befe54db401e8ed0ecb9d52aec700fa67b2972f confine local images in create and form input\r\n* c1db2d55c0826689a129012fbac5a25d5fd3a39f honor configured decode limits across stream consumers\r\n\r\n",
